"""TPS48000HighSideSwitch: reusable high-side N-FET load switch, TPS48000QDGXQ1 controller and ISC035N10NM5LF2 FET,
with an external Kelvin high-side shunt (WSK2512-LOW) for short-circuit protection.

Power path: BUS_IN -> SHUNT (I1 = BUS_IN, I2 = DRAIN; CS+ on the BUS_IN-side tap E1, CS- on the drain-side tap E2)
-> Q1 drain; Q1 source = SRC = BUS_OUT. Positive current flows BUS_IN -> BUS_OUT (DS Fig 7-5 p.16; spec.md Block
definition). The controller VS pin and the UVLO/OV ladder sit on BUS_IN; the charge pump (BST) is across SRC.

io: BUS_IN, BUS_OUT (power path), EN (active high, drives INP), FAULT_N (open drain, FLT), PGOOD_N (open drain,
FLT_GD, active low: low when the FET is fully enhanced), V3V3 (pull-up rail for FAULT_N and PGOOD_N only), GND.

config: rshunt, rshunt_tol, riscp, ctmr, rtmr, rtmr_fitted, rgate, cgate, r_damp, r_top, r_mid, r_bot, fault_pullup,
pgood_pullup, ambient (optional Temperature range), derate (float, default 1.0). Configs change values and DNP only;
topology is fixed. All values come from the block's analysis and the board's params (spec.md Config table).

Instances: U (TPS48000QDGXQ1), Q1 (ISC035N10NM5LF2), SHUNT (WSK2512-LOW), R_ISCP, C_TMR, R_TMR, R_GATE, C_GATE,
R_DAMP, C_BST, C_VS, C_SRC, R_TOP, R_MID, R_BOT, R_FAULT, R_PGOOD.

Gate network (DS Fig 7-4 p.15): PU -> R1 -> gate; PD tied to the gate; gate -> R2 -> C1 -> GND. C1 returns to GND, not
SRC (designer correction D12). Gate, PU and BST nets are declared relative to SRC (BUS_OUT plus the abs-max window to
SRC, DS p.5); the C1 node is declared against GND. Quiescent and timing values are not checked here; the analysis
(blocks/TPS48000HighSideSwitch/analysis.py) owns them.
"""

load("@stdlib/units.zen", "Capacitance", "Resistance", "Temperature", "Voltage")

TPS = Module("github.com/kb1lqc/zener-library/components/TexasInstruments/TPS48000QDGXQ1/TPS48000QDGXQ1.zen")
ISC = Module("github.com/kb1lqc/zener-library/components/Infineon/ISC035N10NM5LF2/ISC035N10NM5LF2.zen")
WSK = Module("github.com/kb1lqc/zener-library/components/Vishay/WSK2512-LOW/WSK2512-LOW.zen")
GCM = Module("github.com/kb1lqc/zener-library/components/Murata/GCM188/GCM188.zen")
GCM21B = Module("github.com/kb1lqc/zener-library/components/Murata/GCM21B/GCM21B.zen")
ERJ = Module("github.com/kb1lqc/zener-library/components/Panasonic/ERJ-3EKF/ERJ-3EKF.zen")

Project(name="TPS48000HighSideSwitch", path="TPS48000HighSideSwitch", layout=False)

BUS_IN = io(Net)
BUS_OUT = io(Net)
# Active high enable; drives the controller INP pin directly.
EN = io(Net)
# Open drain, active low (FLT).
FAULT_N = io(Net)
# Open drain, active low (FLT_GD): low when the FET is fully enhanced.
PGOOD_N = io(Net)
# Pull-up rail for FAULT_N and PGOOD_N. Plain Net so the sub-sheet draws a local hierarchical label.
V3V3 = io(Net)
# Plain Net for the same reason; the cast below re-types it for library pins that require Ground.
GND = io(Net)
_GND = Ground(GND)

rshunt = config(Resistance, help="Shunt resistance, an orderable WSK2512-LOW value for the chosen rshunt_tol")
rshunt_tol = config(str, help="WSK2512-LOW tolerance code: D (+/-0.5 %) or F (+/-1.0 %); from the block analysis")
riscp = config(Resistance, help="ISCP resistor to GND; sets V(SCP) through the library vscp_from_riscp")
ctmr = config(Capacitance, help="Fault-timer capacitor, TMR to GND")
rtmr = config(Resistance, default="100kohm", help="Latch-off resistor across CTMR (DS p.19)")
rtmr_fitted = config(bool, default=True, help="Fit RTMR; False = DNP (fault behaviour changes, topology does not)")
rgate = config(Resistance, help="Gate ramp resistor R1, PU to the gate")
cgate = config(Capacitance, help="Gate ramp capacitor C1, gate to GND (DS Fig 7-4 p.15)")
r_damp = config(Resistance, default="10ohm", help="Damping resistor R2, in series with cgate (DS p.16, Fig 7-4 p.15)")
r_top = config(Resistance, help="UVLO/OV ladder: BUS_IN to EN/UVLO (DS Fig 7-5 p.16)")
r_mid = config(Resistance, help="UVLO/OV ladder: EN/UVLO to OV (DS Fig 7-5 p.16)")
r_bot = config(Resistance, help="UVLO/OV ladder: OV to GND (DS Fig 7-5 p.16)")
fault_pullup = config(bool, default=True, help="Fit the FAULT_N pull-up to V3V3; False when the host supplies one")
pgood_pullup = config(bool, default=True, help="Fit the PGOOD_N pull-up to V3V3; False when the host supplies one")
ambient = config(Temperature, optional=True, help="Board ambient temperature range")
derate = config(float, default=1.0, help="Project derating factor in (0, 1]; shrinks abs-max only")
# Worst-case pin-pair voltages from the block analysis (values.json). Optional: unset, the wrappers fall back to the
# independent net ranges, which fail on a wide bus. Bench values are in bench.zen with their keys.
v_vgs = config(Voltage, optional=True, help="Range of V(G) - V(S), values.json v_vgs_range")
v_abs_cs_pair = config(
    Voltage, optional=True, help="Range of V(CS+) - V(CS-), both fault directions (D10), values.json v_cs_pair_range"
)
v_vds_rating = config(Voltage, optional=True, help="Range of V(D) - V(S) in operation, values.json v_vds_range")
v_shunt_across = config(Voltage, optional=True, help="Shunt voltage, normal operation at the 6 A design current")
v_rdamp_across = config(Voltage, optional=True, help="Voltage across R_DAMP, DC, values.json v_rdamp_dc")

# The wrappers' optional ambient config rejects None, so pass it only when the board sets it.
_AMB = {"ambient": ambient} if ambient != None else {}
# Pin-pair and shunt voltages, passed only when the board sets them (same pattern as ambient).
_VGS = {"v_vgs": v_vgs} if v_vgs != None else {}
_VDS = {"v_vds_rating": v_vds_rating} if v_vds_rating != None else {}
_CSP = {"v_abs_cs_pair": v_abs_cs_pair} if v_abs_cs_pair != None else {}
_VSH = {"v_across": v_shunt_across} if v_shunt_across != None else {}
_VRD = {"v_across": v_rdamp_across} if v_rdamp_across != None else {}

# Internal nets. Voltages are declared as bounds (see the module docstring); the shunt and FET drain follow BUS_IN.
DRAIN = Net(voltage=BUS_IN.voltage)
# Shunt taps: CS+ on the BUS_IN-side tap (E1), CS- on the drain-side tap (E2).
CS_P = Net(voltage=BUS_IN.voltage)
CS_N = Net(voltage=BUS_IN.voltage)
# Gate, PU and BST nets: SRC (up to 40 V, the rated bus) plus the abs-max window to SRC (-0.3 V to 19 V, DS p.5).
# Declared as absolute bounds because the module cannot read the caller voltage of BUS_OUT at definition time.
GATE = Net(voltage="-0.3V to 59V")
PU_NET = Net(voltage="-0.3V to 59V")
BST_NET = Net(voltage="-0.3V to 59V")
# C1 node (R2 to C1): C1 returns to GND, so this node sees the gate voltage against GND (up to the bus maximum plus
# V(BST-SRC) max, 53.86 V, values.json v_c1_max_v). Declared at 59 V, above that, and inside the 100 V C0G rating.
C1_NODE = Net(voltage="-0.3V to 59V")
# Controller timing and set-point pins, bounded by the ISCP/TMR abs-max row (DS p.5).
ISCP_NET = Net(voltage="-0.3V to 5.5V")
TMR_NET = Net(voltage="-0.3V to 5.5V")
# UVLO/OV divider nodes: between 0 and the bus maximum (the divider never exceeds BUS_IN).
EN_NODE = Net(voltage="0V to 40V")
OV_NODE = Net(voltage="0V to 40V")

U = TPS(
    name="U",
    EN_UVLO=EN_NODE,
    OV=OV_NODE,
    INP=EN,
    FLT_GD=PGOOD_N,
    FLT=FAULT_N,
    GND=_GND,
    CS_SEL=_GND,
    ISCP=ISCP_NET,
    TMR=TMR_NET,
    SCP_TEST=_GND,
    BST=BST_NET,
    SRC=BUS_OUT,
    PD=GATE,
    PU=PU_NET,
    CS_N=CS_N,
    CS_P=CS_P,
    VS=BUS_IN,
    derate=derate,
    **dict(_AMB, **_CSP),
)

Q1 = ISC(
    name="Q1",
    S=BUS_OUT,
    G=GATE,
    D=DRAIN,
    derate=derate,
    **dict(_VGS, **_VDS),
)

SHUNT = WSK(
    name="SHUNT",
    value=rshunt,
    tolerance=rshunt_tol,
    I1=BUS_IN,
    I2=DRAIN,
    E1=CS_P,
    E2=CS_N,
    derate=derate,
    **dict(_AMB, **_VSH),
)

# ISCP set-point resistor to GND (V(SCP) from RISCP).
R_ISCP = ERJ(name="R_ISCP", value=riscp, P1=ISCP_NET, P2=_GND, derate=derate, **_AMB)

# Fault timer: CTMR, and the latch-off resistor RTMR across it (DS p.19). C0G so the timer tolerance is not temperature
# or DC-bias dependent.
C_TMR = GCM(
    name="C_TMR",
    value=ctmr,
    rated_v="100V",
    dielectric="C0G",
    tolerance="+/-5%",
    P1=TMR_NET,
    P2=_GND,
    derate=derate,
    **_AMB,
)
R_TMR = ERJ(name="R_TMR", value=rtmr, P1=TMR_NET, P2=_GND, dnp=not rtmr_fitted, derate=derate, **_AMB)

# Gate ramp (DS Fig 7-4 p.15): PU -> R1 -> gate; PD tied to the gate (fast turn-off, DS p.16); gate -> R2 -> C1 -> GND.
R_GATE = ERJ(name="R_GATE", value=rgate, P1=PU_NET, P2=GATE, derate=derate, **_AMB)
R_DAMP = ERJ(name="R_DAMP", value=r_damp, P1=GATE, P2=C1_NODE, derate=derate, **dict(_AMB, **_VRD))
# C1 sees V(gate - GND) up to the bus maximum plus V(BST-SRC) max (eq. 3 / eq. 4, DS p.16). 100 V C0G (designer D13).
C_GATE = GCM(
    name="C_GATE",
    value=cgate,
    rated_v="100V",
    dielectric="C0G",
    tolerance="+/-5%",
    P1=C1_NODE,
    P2=_GND,
    derate=derate,
    **_AMB,
)

# Charge pump (DS eq. 4, p.16): one X7R 470 nF 0805, BST to SRC (designer decision D14: 470 nF tolerates more than 50 %
# DC-bias loss; the minimum is in values.json cbst_min_nf).
C_BST = GCM21B(
    name="C_BST",
    value="470nF",
    rated_v="50V",
    dielectric="X7R",
    tolerance="+/-10%",
    P1=BST_NET,
    P2=BUS_OUT,
    derate=derate,
    **_AMB,
)

# Decoupling: 100 nF at VS (to GND) and at SRC (to GND).
C_VS = GCM(
    name="C_VS",
    value="100nF",
    rated_v="50V",
    dielectric="X7R",
    tolerance="+/-10%",
    P1=BUS_IN,
    P2=_GND,
    derate=derate,
    **_AMB,
)
C_SRC = GCM(
    name="C_SRC",
    value="100nF",
    rated_v="50V",
    dielectric="X7R",
    tolerance="+/-10%",
    P1=BUS_OUT,
    P2=_GND,
    derate=derate,
    **_AMB,
)

# UVLO/OV ladder: BUS_IN -> r_top -> EN/UVLO -> r_mid -> OV -> r_bot -> GND (DS Fig 7-5 p.16, eq. 12, 13).
R_TOP = ERJ(name="R_TOP", value=r_top, P1=BUS_IN, P2=EN_NODE, derate=derate, **_AMB)
R_MID = ERJ(name="R_MID", value=r_mid, P1=EN_NODE, P2=OV_NODE, derate=derate, **_AMB)
R_BOT = ERJ(name="R_BOT", value=r_bot, P1=OV_NODE, P2=_GND, derate=derate, **_AMB)

# Open-drain pull-ups to V3V3 (DNP-able). 10 kohm, as on INA229HighSideMonitor.
R_FAULT = ERJ(name="R_FAULT", value="10kohm", P1=FAULT_N, P2=V3V3, dnp=not fault_pullup, derate=derate, **_AMB)
R_PGOOD = ERJ(name="R_PGOOD", value="10kohm", P1=PGOOD_N, P2=V3V3, dnp=not pgood_pullup, derate=derate, **_AMB)
